{"clock":1,"nonce":"2e8e0dad986861434d822cdf6ecc1d87","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792679423,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5981348114"},"data":{"body":"ADR 0001 keeps each check's result as a signed line in `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e`. M4 (#46) writes and verifies them, but nothing moves them: a proof never leaves the machine that ran it, so a reviewer who pulls the repository finds none. The ADR's goal, async first (\"a reviewer pulls the repo, checks the status and trusts the check\"), needs this.\n\nThe ADR's section 2 sets the rules:\n- a clone pushes only its own `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e`, which only fast-forwards;\n- it fetches the other writers' refs into `refs/notes/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/ci/*`, never with a `+` into its own namespace;\n- a reader takes the union of every writer's ref;\n- pushes go with git-board's sync, not one per run.\n\n\n- git-board's sync pushes this clone's `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e` and fetches every other writer's into `refs/notes/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/ci/*`.\n- A check proven in one clone reads as proven in a second clone once both have synced, and `git board verify` agrees there.\n- A push of the clone's own ref that doesn't fast-forward is reported, never forced.\n- The verdict reads the remote-tracking refs as well as the local ones.\n- docs/ says how a reviewer without git-board fetches the notes (one refspec) and verifies a check with git and ssh-keygen.\n- Tested with throwaway repositories, never live remotes.","title":"proof: sync refs/notes/ci, so a reviewer pulls the proofs"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792679427,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5981348114"},"data":{"add":["kind:feat","prio:p0","status:ready","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}}]}